  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are the statements about diborane<br />(a) Diborane is prepared by the oxidation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaBH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br />(b) Each boron atom is in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybridized state<br />(c) Diborane has one bridged <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> centre-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-electron bond<br />(d) Diborane is a planar molecule</p><p>The option with correct statement(s) is&nbsp;</p>",
