  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Diborane is prepared by the reaction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaBH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NaBH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NaI</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br />In diborane, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridized. It is non-planar molecule and it has two <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math> bonds.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c768c459-1eff-411b-ba20-b18658a47240-image.png\" style=\"width: 435px; height: 143px;\" /></p>",
